---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<div class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>Tools</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">
				Curated tools to speed up daily work.
			</p>
		</header>

		<h2>Session managment</h2>

		<p>Make sure you have shit+enter configured to go to a new line (setup instructions) (/terminal-setup)</p>
		<p>Check your usage (claude /usage, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>Check your current context usage (claude /context, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>Clear your context / start a new session (claude /clear, same for copilot)</p>
		<p>How to interrupt the current (claude ctrl+c or ESC, same for copilot)</p>

		<h2>Prompting</h2>

		<p>Referenceing specific files, use the @ symbol, then select the file with up and down error. These files will be added to your context. (same for copilot)</p>

		<p>You can stash a command with ctrl+s. After the next command you get your stased command back. (does not exist in copilot)</p>

		<p>Copy & Paste images into the CLI. Does not work in WSL. (needs checking, on native)</p>

		<h2>GHCP Cli and VSCode</h2>

		<p>Connect to your IDE via /ide. This allows you to view diffs directly in your IDE, rather than a regular diff in the terminal (/ide, same for GHCP CLI)</p>


		<h2>Time travel</h2>

		<p>ESC + ESC to enter the time travel mode. Now you can select where to go and how to go there,
			Restore code and conversation, Restore conversation (code will be unchanged), Restore code (conversation will be unchanged). (same in GHCP without the options, /undo /rewind)</p>

		<p>Resuming sessions - exit claude code and resume by running `claude --resume <session-id>` (same for GHCP CLI)</p>
		<p>Can not remember your session id? `claude --continue` (same for GHCP CLI)</p>
		<p>Start claude without parameters, /resume (same for GHCP CLI)</p>

		<h2>Bash commands?!</h2>
		<p>Running a shell command - ! to enter the bash mode. CTRL+B to run a command (like a dev server in the background). Arrow keys to get back to that background session (GHCP CLI ! to enter shell mode, no way to return to running processes?! needs investigation)</p>

		<p>CTRL + Z + fg</p>

		<h2>Permissions</h2>

		<p>Permissions are stored in .claude/settings.local.json (GHCP CLI ~/.copilot/permissions-config.json)</p>
		<p>Permissions can be shared in a team with .claude/settings.json (GHCP CLI does not support this)</p>

	</div>
</Layout>
